# 28. Troubleshooting Reference

| Problem | Investigation |
|---|---|
| Interface is DOWN | `ip link show` |
| Incorrect IP address | `ip -br addr` |
| Incorrect gateway | `ip route` |
| Neighbor is STALE | `ip neigh show` |
| Ping requests arrive but replies are missing | tcpdump and iptables |
| ICMP Echo ignored | `cat /proc/sys/net/ipv4/icmp_echo_ignore_all` |
| Routing problems | `ip route show table all` |
| Policy-routing problems | `ip rule show` |
| Public IP works but hostname fails | DNS configuration |

# 29. Important Notes for Repeating This Practical

1. Both VMs must be connected to the same NAT Network.
2. Keep the IP addresses unique.
3. If DHCP is disabled, configure static IP addresses manually.
4. Android interface name in this lab is `wifi_eth`.
5. Kali interface name in this lab is `eth0`.
6. Android root commands must be executed after `su`.
7. The Android IP, routes, policy rules and firewall modifications made through the terminal may not persist after reboot.
8. Verify the configuration instead of assuming it has persisted.
9. The routing recovery commands documented above reproduce the configuration used in this lab; do not apply them blindly to other networks.
10. Avoid leaving permissive firewall settings enabled outside the isolated practical.

