# 31. Conclusion

The practical involved installing Android-x86 9.0-r2 in Oracle VirtualBox and connecting it to Kali Linux through a shared NAT Network.

Initially, communication between the machines was inconsistent. I investigated IP addressing, ARP, routing, ICMP, packet captures and firewall rules.

After experimenting with the routing and firewall configurations, I established successful bidirectional communication between the two virtual machines.

I also corrected Android's default routing and policy-routing configuration, allowing it to access the internet.

Finally, both Android and Kali successfully reached 8.8.8.8 and resolved google.com.

This practical provided hands-on experience in virtual networking, Linux networking, routing, packet analysis, firewall troubleshooting and DNS.

